and the resulting file PARSES.  A STRICT `git apply` (no flag) fails at line 908.  The cause is line-ending
normalisation in the scratch harness, not content: the stacked file is 100% CRLF, the generated diff's
context lines are not, and `--ignore-whitespace` is exactly the flag for that.  BOTH anchor blocks below
occur EXACTLY ONCE in the stacked file, so there is no ambiguity about where this applies.  If the strict
apply fails on the real tree too, use the deterministic fallback below rather than forcing the patch.

DETERMINISTIC FALLBACK (two exact, unique search/replace blocks -- this is the authoritative statement of
the change; the unified diff below is a convenience):
  BLOCK 1 -- find, exactly once:
        ev_by[(e.sent_idx, e.pred_idx)].append(e)
    for si, s in enumerate(chunk):
  ... and insert the seven `unit_state_items` / `unit_model_props` lines (with their comment) between the
  two, as shown in the + lines of hunk 1.
  BLOCK 2 -- find, exactly once, the three lines
            holders = [h for (h, p, ty) in gold_states]
            shuf = list(holders)
            rng.shuffle(shuf)
  ... and the `for k, (h, p, ty) in enumerate(gold_states):` loop that follows, and replace them as shown in
  hunk 2: drop the sentence-scoped shuffle, append each item to `unit_state_items`, and score the twin after
  the sentence loop.

WHAT IS WRONG, WITH THE NUMBER THAT FOUND IT.  The `state` row's information-free TWIN shuffles the gold
holders WITHIN ONE SENTENCE.  A sentence with a single predicational clause -- the common case -- hands the
holder back to itself, so the twin IS the model.  Measured on the sealed modern holdout (279 documents, 139
state items): model 0.7410, twin 0.6906, model - twin +0.0504 [+0.0142,+0.0981].  Only ~5% of items ever
received a different holder, so the state row's "the twin loses" check is close to vacuous.  It is NOT a
property of short documents: the chunk-matched arm (8 sealed documents concatenated, identical token
stream) reproduces the twin at 0.6906 EXACTLY, because the shuffle is sentence-scoped, not unit-scoped.

THE FIX.  Collect the unit's state items during the sentence loop and score the twin AFTER it, permuting the
holders ACROSS the whole scoring unit (with a derangement attempt so a holder is not handed back to itself).
The `model` and `most_recent_noun` arms are untouched item-for-item, so no published model or floor number
moves; only the twin becomes genuinely information-free.

SCORER VERSION MARKER (strategy instruction, phase 7).  The landing record must carry the marker as a FIELD,
not only as the comment this patch adds: records written before this change are `state_twin_scorer: "v1"`
(sentence-scoped shuffle), after it `"v2"`.  v1 and v2 state twins are NOT comparable and must never be
plotted on one series.  The one v1 record on disk is
data/exp_sealed_modern_holdout_v1/board_landings.jsonl line 1 (2026-09-16, state twin 0.6906).

RISK OF THIS RECOMMENDATION, STATED.  It will LOWER the published state twin and therefore WIDEN the state
model-minus-twin margin on every population, sealed and read.  That is a number moving in the flattering
direction because a control was made stricter, and it must be reported that way, not as a gain.

NOT VERIFIED BY A RUN.  The patched copy parses and the edit is mechanical, but it has NOT been executed:
running it needs the strategy session to land it and re-run the board.

